@* One design token, shown as the color it resolves to.

   No value text beside it, unlike the React guide: reading a resolved custom property needs
   getComputedStyle, and this library stays JS-free so it renders in both hosts and under bUnit.
   The chip is drawn with the token itself, so it is still the live value. *@

<div class="sg-swatch">
    <div class="sg-chip" style="background: var(--color-@Token);"></div>
    <code>--color-@Token</code>
</div>

@code {
    [Parameter, EditorRequired]
    public string Token { get; set; } = string.Empty;
}
